msgid "Technical discussion {#technical-discussion}"
msgstr "Perbincangan teknikal {#technical-discussion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "System sizes and computational requirements {#system-sizes-and-computational-requirements}"
msgstr "Saiz sistem dan keperluan pengiraan {#system-sizes-and-computational-requirements}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The computational cost of SQD is dominated by the eigenstate solver calls. At each step of the self-consistent configuration recovery iteration, n\\_batches of eigenstate solver calls are performed. The different calls are embarrassingly parallel. In this [tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization), those calls are inside a for loop. **It is highly recommended to perform these calls in parallel**.\n"
msgstr "Kos pengiraan SQD didominasi oleh panggilan penyelesai keadaan eigen. Pada setiap langkah lelaran pemulihan konfigurasi swakonsisten, n\\_batches panggilan penyelesai keadaan eigen dilaksanakan. Panggilan-panggilan yang berbeza ini adalah selari secara memalukan (embarrassingly parallel). Dalam [tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization) ini, panggilan tersebut berada di dalam gelung for. **Anda sangat disyorkan melaksanakan panggilan ini secara selari**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion\") function is multithreaded and capable of handling systems with \\~25 spacial orbitals and \\~10 electrons with subspace dimensions of \\~\\$10^7\\$, using \\~10-30 cores.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion\") ialah berbilang-thread dan mampu mengendalikan sistem dengan \\~25 orbital ruang dan \\~10 elektron dengan dimensi subruang \\~\\$10^7\\$, menggunakan \\~10-30 teras.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing subspace dimensions {#choosing-subspace-dimensions}"
msgstr "Memilih dimensi subruang {#choosing-subspace-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of the subspace dimension affects the accuracy and runtime of the eigenstate solver. The larger the subspace, the more accurate the calculation, at the cost of increasing the runtime and memory requirements. The optimal subspace size of a given system is not known; thus, a convergence study with the subspace dimension can be performed, as described in this [guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension).\n"
msgstr "Pilihan dimensi subruang mempengaruhi ketepatan dan masa jalan penyelesai keadaan eigen. Semakin besar subruang, semakin tepat pengiraan, dengan kos peningkatan masa jalan dan keperluan memori. Saiz subruang optimum bagi sesuatu sistem tidak diketahui; oleh itu, kajian penumpuan dengan dimensi subruang boleh dilakukan, seperti yang diterangkan dalam [panduan](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bounding the subspace dimension {#bounding-the-subspace-dimension}"
msgstr "Menghadkan dimensi subruang {#bounding-the-subspace-dimension}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `samples_per_batch` argument of [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") sets the number of bitstrings contained in each batch, and thereby controls the subspace dimension indirectly: in the case of quantum chemistry applications, its value sets an upper bound to the subspace dimension. The dimension that actually results depends on how many of the sampled bitstrings are distinct, and it grows over the course of the self-consistent configuration recovery iterations, so it is not known in advance. See this [example](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Argumen `samples_per_batch` bagi [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") menetapkan bilangan bitstring dalam setiap kelompok, dan dengan itu mengawal dimensi subruang secara tidak langsung: dalam kes aplikasi kimia kuantum, nilainya menetapkan had atas bagi dimensi subruang. Dimensi yang sebenarnya terhasil bergantung pada berapa banyak bitstring yang disampel adalah berbeza, dan ia bertambah sepanjang lelaran pemulihan konfigurasi swakonsisten, jadi ia tidak diketahui lebih awal. Lihat [contoh](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell) ini untuk butiran lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `max_dim` argument of the same function bounds the dimension directly, by limiting the number of CI strings retained in each spin sector. Since the subspace is spanned by the Cartesian product of the two spin sectors, `max_dim=d` caps the subspace dimension at `d**2`, while a tuple `max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` limits the spin-alpha and spin-beta sectors separately, capping the subspace dimension at `d_a * d_b` (with `symmetrize_spin=True`, the two limits must be equal). When a batch yields more CI strings than the limit allows, the strings requested through `include_configurations` and those carried over from the previous iteration are retained preferentially, and the remaining slots are filled with the most frequently sampled strings. Because it caps the size of the largest diagonalization that the eigenstate solver will be asked to perform, `max_dim` is a convenient way to keep the solver within a runtime and memory budget. See this [guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Argumen `max_dim` bagi fungsi yang sama menghadkan dimensi secara langsung, dengan mengehadkan bilangan rentetan CI yang dikekalkan dalam setiap sektor spin. Memandangkan subruang dijanakan oleh hasil darab Cartesian bagi dua sektor spin, `max_dim=d` menghadkan dimensi subruang kepada `d**2`, manakala tuple `max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` mengehadkan sektor spin-alfa dan spin-beta secara berasingan, menghadkan dimensi subruang kepada `d_a * d_b` (dengan `symmetrize_spin=True`, kedua-dua had mesti sama). Apabila satu kelompok menghasilkan lebih banyak rentetan CI daripada yang dibenarkan oleh had, rentetan yang diminta melalui `include_configurations` dan yang dibawa daripada lelaran sebelumnya dikekalkan secara keutamaan, dan baki slot diisi dengan rentetan yang paling kerap disampel. Kerana ia menghadkan saiz pepenyahdiagonalan terbesar yang akan diminta daripada penyelesai keadaan eigen, `max_dim` ialah cara yang mudah untuk mengekalkan penyelesai dalam bajet masa jalan dan memori. Lihat [panduan](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) ini untuk butiran lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solvers {#solvers}"
msgstr "Penyelesai {#solvers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projection and diagonalization steps are performed by a classical solver. We provide here two generic solvers, one for Fermionic systems and another for qubit systems. Other solvers that might be more efficient for specific systems can be interfaced by the users.\n"
msgstr "Langkah unjuran dan pepenyahdiagonalan dilakukan oleh penyelesai klasik. Kami menyediakan di sini dua penyelesai generik, satu untuk sistem Fermionik dan satu lagi untuk sistem qubit. Penyelesai lain yang mungkin lebih cekap untuk sistem tertentu boleh disambungkan oleh pengguna.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trim SQD {#trim-sqd}"
msgstr "Trim SQD {#trim-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Standard SQD diagonalizes each subsampled batch independently and keeps the best result, so the number of configurations it can consider is limited to what one affordable subspace can hold. **Trim SQD** instead partitions the bitstrings into batches, performs an intermediate diagonalization of each batch, then performs a larger diagonalization using the highest-weight determinants from each partition. This method is based on joint research from the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM [\\[7\\]](#references), and can be enabled by passing a [`TrimPolicy`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/trim#qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy \"qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy\") object to the [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") function.\n"
msgstr "SQD standard mendiagonalkan setiap kelompok subsampel secara bebas dan mengekalkan hasil terbaik, jadi bilangan konfigurasi yang boleh dipertimbangkan terhad kepada apa yang boleh dimuatkan oleh satu subruang yang mampu milik. **Trim SQD** sebaliknya membahagikan bitstring kepada kelompok, melakukan pepenyahdiagonalan perantaraan bagi setiap kelompok, kemudian melakukan pepenyahdiagonalan yang lebih besar menggunakan determinan berpemberat tertinggi daripada setiap partisi. Kaedah ini berdasarkan penyelidikan bersama daripada Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, dan IBM [\\[7\\]](#references), dan boleh didayakan dengan menghantar objek [`TrimPolicy`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/trim#qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy \"qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy\") kepada fungsi [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\").\n"

